<ExportGuideLayout
  title="How to Export Your Students from Kicksite"
  description="Export your student list and ranks from Kicksite as CSV files and import them into BeltManager, step by step. Sourced from Kicksite's own help pages, checked November 2026."
  heading="How to export your students from Kicksite"
  crumb="Export from Kicksite"
  locale="us"
  checked="November 6, 2026"
  ctaHeading="Ready to bring your school across?"
  sources={[
    { label: 'Kicksite Help Center: Tip: How Do I Print PINs for Student Attendance Check In?', url: 'https://kicksite.com/knowledge-base/tip-how-do-i-print-pins-for-student-attendance-check-in/', note: 'Updated September 23, 2025. Read November 6, 2026. The student list export is described here as part of printing PINs.' },
    { label: 'Kicksite Help Center: How to Use the Programs Section', url: 'https://kicksite.com/knowledge-base/programs-section/', note: 'Updated August 29, 2024. Read November 6, 2026.' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    You can download your Kicksite student list as a CSV from the web portal. These steps come from Kicksite's help center. We haven't
    run them in a Kicksite account.
  </p>
  <h2>Export your students</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>In the left panel, choose <strong>Profiles</strong>, then <strong>Students</strong>.</li>
    <li>Check the <strong>Status</strong> filter. It shows only active students by default, which is what you want for this import.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Export</strong>. A CSV file downloads.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Export your ranks</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>In the left sidebar, choose <strong>Programs</strong>, then <strong>Ranks Overview</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Export</strong>. This downloads a CSV of the students in each rank.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    If your student file has no rank column, copy each student's rank from this second file into a new column called Current belt.
    BeltManager imports one file at a time.
  </p>
  <h2>What the file contains</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Kicksite's help pages don't list every column in the student export.</strong> The article above names First Name and Last Name
    and shows that the file runs out to column AI. Open it before you import and look for date of birth, which BeltManager
    requires, and for guardian details, which every student under 18 needs.
  </p>
</ExportGuideLayout>
